  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Dong Fang Chang Fan tells Tan Bi Ya that snowy mountain blessed land has already secretly contacted Ma tribe to give them support. Tan Bi Ya names that group as demonic path Gu Immortals. She already knows the group has long coveted Eighty-Eight True Yang Building and is backing Ma tribe for Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        514
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_dong_fang_chang_fan",
        "char_tan_bi_ya",
        "fac_ma_tribe",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "inh_giant_sun_immortal_venerable_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A lofty Snowy Mountain stands tall and reaches through the clouds. This is a spotlessly white region, and even the buildings on the mountain are carved out of ice crystals.",
      "chapters": [
        537
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tens of northern plains demonic path Gu Immortals occupy different peaks there. On one peak, Xue Song Zi holds Xue Song Pavilion and a branch peak of his own.",
      "chapters": [
        537
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-peaks",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xue_song_zi",
        "loc_xue_song_pavilion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Snowy Mountain blessed land has fifteen snowy peaks in total. Mu Ling Lan tells its ninth peak lord Hair Mistress that rank eight Gu Immortals are following his group of five Central Continent immortals, and that the blessed land, for all its territorial advantage, holds only one rank eight in the end. He is bluffing, since the outcome for the immortals left behind in the spaceless tunnel bodes ill rather than well, and his five may be the only ones saved. Hair Mistress tells the five that a super Gu formation there uses the snowy peak lords as its formation cores and links to Reverse Flow River. By her telling it lifts every defending peak lord, so that rank six cultivation shows rank seven strength, while it greatly suppresses whoever charges a peak. Her one strand of hair, risen as a dam, blocks Mu Ling Lan’s water wave and bears that account out.",
      "chapters": [
        1250
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fifteen-peaks-and-the-super-gu-formation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mu_ling_lan",
        "char_hair_mistress",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "sys_super_gu_formation",
        "loc_reverse_flow_river"
      ]
    }
  ],
